  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Giant boulders move across this dry lakebed all by themselves. Deep trails stretch behind rocks weighing seven hundred pounds.",
        "visual_keywords": "cracked dry lakebed desert"
      },
      {
        "narration": "For decades, fresh tracks appeared every winter. Yet nobody ever caught a single stone in motion.",
        "visual_keywords": "barren mountain valley sunset"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Were the stones breaking physics? Researchers finally bolted custom GPS trackers directly to the rocks and waited.",
        "visual_keywords": "close up rocks desert"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Rare winter rain formed thin ice sheets around the stones. Morning sun thawed the ice into floating panels, letting light breezes push the heavy rocks over slick mud.",
        "visual_keywords": "sun melting ice water"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2014, high-speed GPS finally solved it. But as Death Valley warms, will these walking rocks ever move again?",
        "visual_keywords": "wide empty desert horizon"
      }
    ],
